WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:18.369 --> 00:00:22.279
Ambassador Hall, I wanted to, I wanted to ask you, you talked about how your inspiration 

00:00:22.279 --> 00:00:26.499
for the fast was this passage in Isaiah fifty eight 

00:00:26.499 --> 00:00:31.289
and this motivated you and this, this, this was such a powerful motivation for you that, 

00:00:31.289 --> 00:00:32.839
that you were willing to end your career over this,

00:00:32.839 --> 00:00:35.150
You were willing to do something you thought, you know, I think this is going to

00:00:35.150 --> 00:00:36.290
put an end to this whole

00:00:36.290 --> 00:00:41.190
this, this whole congress thing all the good I feel like I'm doing here I'm willing to sacrifice any of that going forward

00:00:41.190 --> 00:00:43.710
because I think this, this is really powerful

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:45.280
and I'm going to this

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:46.830
and then you went and, and 

00:00:46.830 --> 00:00:48.220
when you told people about this

00:00:48.220 --> 00:00:49.920
and you said you were doing this 

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:50.620
you said you, you didn't tell them your motivation

00:00:50.620 --> 00:00:52.540
because you, you said

00:00:52.540 --> 00:00:55.020
that they would've thought you were crazy.

00:00:55.020 --> 00:01:00.860
The questions I have are 1)

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:05.519
can, can you envision a world in, in which you would've told them and, and, and 2) 

00:01:05.519 --> 00:01:09.150
do you think that's a good place for us to
be? I mean is, is that the direction,

00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:11.370
it seems to me this class has kind of, 

00:01:11.370 --> 00:01:14.810
it's kind of what we're talking about is getting to that sort of direction where we can say 

00:01:14.810 --> 00:01:16.600
my faith wants me to do, you know,

00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:19.130
my faith motivates me to alleviate poverty and I'm going to share

00:01:19.130 --> 00:01:21.670
with you my faith-based reasons as

00:01:21.670 --> 00:01:22.890
well as my, you know, 

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:24.620
less faith-based reasons for, for alleviating 

00:01:24.620 --> 00:01:31.620
poverty or for doing something else good.

00:01:31.640 --> 00:01:32.700
I didn't

00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:34.490
when I announced

00:01:34.490 --> 00:01:39.399
that I was going to do this have a fast I,
I didn't say my inspiration was Isaiah fifty

00:01:39.399 --> 00:01:40.510
eight 

00:01:40.510 --> 00:01:42.560
but when asked

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:43.320
why

00:01:43.320 --> 00:01:45.980
would I do this

00:01:45.980 --> 00:01:48.290
I, I didn't hesitate

00:01:48.290 --> 00:01:50.370
and

00:01:50.370 --> 00:01:55.549
I didn't want to, I didn't, but I didn't, I've
seen so many elected officials use

00:01:55.549 --> 00:01:58.500
faith in such a way that it was

00:01:58.500 --> 00:02:00.410
odious to me

00:02:00.410 --> 00:02:02.420
and I didn't want to be that, but

00:02:02.420 --> 00:02:04.130
I would often say

00:02:04.130 --> 00:02:05.429
people were also

00:02:05.429 --> 00:02:06.520
ask me

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:12.099
not only in my district but reporters
and staff I'd say "Well turn off your camera.

00:02:12.099 --> 00:02:15.889
Let's talk" and I would talk to them about faith
and I'd tell them

00:02:15.889 --> 00:02:18.779
you know my personal belief and why.

00:02:18.779 --> 00:02:23.569
So, I never denied it and matter of fact there
were several articles on it, but

00:02:23.569 --> 00:02:25.870
only if asked

00:02:25.870 --> 00:02:29.760
because I believe if you try to push faith
and religion down people's throats people

00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:32.590
will run and they will get mad and, and

00:02:32.590 --> 00:02:35.299
it's it's not necessary

00:02:35.299 --> 00:02:39.869
because God is a big God, he can take care
of himself.

00:02:39.869 --> 00:02:41.309
I learned this lesson from my wife.

00:02:43.229 --> 00:02:46.619
When I first became a believer I tried to
the shove

00:02:46.619 --> 00:02:48.709
my faith down her throat

00:02:48.709 --> 00:02:51.569
in that every night I would say "Jan,

00:02:51.569 --> 00:02:56.659
would you like to receive Jesus tonight?"

00:02:56.659 --> 00:02:59.749
You can imagine how far this went and

00:02:59.749 --> 00:03:03.900
my friends would come over and they'd say "Tony,
what's new?" And I'd say "You're not going to believe this 

00:03:03.900 --> 00:03:05.669
but I,

00:03:05.669 --> 00:03:09.790
I believe in Jesus." And they "Oh my gosh." And 

00:03:09.790 --> 00:03:12.919
my wife would kick me under the table 

00:03:12.919 --> 00:03:15.509
and everybody would look up to the ceiling

00:03:15.509 --> 00:03:16.609
and

00:03:16.609 --> 00:03:19.279
my wife said "You're not going to have any
friends.

00:03:19.279 --> 00:03:23.609
What are you, are you a nut case?

00:03:23.609 --> 00:03:27.009
So, after six months of asking her,

00:03:27.009 --> 00:03:31.519
she, I stopped because I was getting nowhere
and she was getting mad at me.

00:03:31.519 --> 00:03:35.899
Six months later then she became a person
of faith after I said nothing.

00:03:35.899 --> 00:03:37.099
I did not nothing.

00:03:37.099 --> 00:03:38.979
I said why did you change.

00:03:38.979 --> 00:03:41.769
She said because when you stop preaching

00:03:41.769 --> 00:03:43.319
and speaking

00:03:43.319 --> 00:03:45.739
and acting like a jerk

00:03:45.739 --> 00:03:47.129
I saw your life change.

00:03:47.129 --> 00:03:50.769
I saw your life change towards me, your children,

00:03:50.769 --> 00:03:52.329
towards your job.

00:03:52.329 --> 00:03:54.689
Said I knew that it was real and it was good

00:03:54.689 --> 00:03:57.279
and I wanted that.

00:03:57.279 --> 00:04:01.529
So, I come at it by learning this lesson from
my wife that you don't

00:04:01.529 --> 00:04:03.329
have to preach it,

00:04:03.329 --> 00:04:04.689
you've just,

00:04:04.689 --> 00:04:05.859
hopefully you show it

00:04:05.859 --> 00:04:08.069
and people will ask you

00:04:08.069 --> 00:04:10.159
what motivates you, you know, they're always
going to ask. Good.

